# CODEOWNERS — who must review what.
#
# Every path listed here can lose real money, either by moving it or by hiding
# that it moved. GitHub requires a review from the listed owner on any PR that
# touches them, provided "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in the
# branch protection rule for main. Without that setting this file is only a
# suggestion, so turn it on (see the gh api command in the PR that added this).
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: ct/strategies/, research/, web/, tests/, docs. A bad
# strategy scores badly and the risk engine still refuses it; a bad chart is
# embarrassing, not expensive. Owning everything means reading nothing.

# The hard gate. Sizing, exposure caps, the cash floor and the edge gate all
# live here, and every entry in the system goes through evaluate(). A one-line
# change here can approve a trade the research says loses money.
# Non-negotiables #1, #2, #4.
/ct/risk.py                       @Squid-Beast

# Binary reject gates, run before any scoring. Deleting one gate is a one-line
# diff that silently widens what the system is willing to buy.
# Non-negotiable #1 (nothing upstream may override the gate chain).
/ct/safety.py                     @Squid-Beast

# The append-only hash-chained audit trail. It is the only record of what
# actually happened; if it can be edited, nothing else in the repo is evidence.
# Non-negotiables #5, #6, #8.
/ct/ledger.py                     @Squid-Beast

# Signs and sends real Solana transactions and decides whether a send confirmed.
# An optimistic confirm() means the system believes it holds something it does
# not, and every later decision rests on that.
# Non-negotiables #6, #7.
/app/executor.py                  @Squid-Beast

# The daemon that decides when to enter and when to exit. Holds the approval
# boundary: manage() must never wait for a human, execute() must always.
# Non-negotiables #1, #3.
/app/service.py                   @Squid-Beast

# Every threshold in the system lives in config, and nowhere else. Editing a
# number here is indistinguishable in effort from a typo and identical in effect
# to rewriting the risk engine.
# Non-negotiables #2, #4.
/config.yaml                      @Squid-Beast
/config-small.yaml                @Squid-Beast

# The rules themselves. If these can be edited without review, every rule above
# is editable without review by first editing this file.
/.claude/rules/non-negotiables.md @Squid-Beast

# The pipeline, including the guards and this file. A PR that weakens a money
# path plus a PR that disables the check that would have caught it is the same
# PR. Owning .github/ means the second half cannot land quietly.
/.github/                         @Squid-Beast
